335
00:30:42,031 --> 00:30:44,950
Rym: Well, the trouble is, they're hitting the problem that every convention runs into.

336
00:30:45,430 --> 00:30:53,813
Rym: There are very few convention center facilities in the United States that accommodate this kind of nerd con.

337
00:30:54,033 --> 00:31:05,481
Scott: Yeah, you can move somewhere else, but then you lose the experience you've built in this building, the relationships you've made in this building, and you lose the population density, you know, radius that you have in Philly.

338
00:31:05,581 --> 00:31:05,883
Scott: Because

339
00:31:05,963 --> 00:31:20,538
Rym: PAX South was very tabletop focused, but PAX South, one, was in a fascist state, which, you know, not safe to go to, and two, PAX South, the only people who could afford to go to it were rich people like us, who go to all the PAXes, or people who live near it.

340
00:31:20,919 --> 00:31:32,492
Rym: But PAX Unplugged is the most diverse PAX by a wide margin, because it is economically financially accessible to a ridiculous number of people.

341
00:31:32,512 --> 00:31:39,177
Scott: Yeah, so moving it kind of will, you know, make it less crowded, so you go to a bigger building that less people can get to.

342
00:31:39,258 --> 00:31:46,708
